# EDA Summary and Observations

## Dataset Overview

The Rice Leaf Disease dataset contains three disease categories:

* Bacterial Leaf Blight
* Brown Spot
* Leaf Smut

During dataset inspection, a total of 119 images were found. The class distribution is as follows:

* Bacterial Leaf Blight: 40 images
* Brown Spot: 40 images
* Leaf Smut: 39 images

Although the project description mentions 120 images, only 119 images were available after extraction. The dataset is nearly balanced, with only one image missing from the Leaf Smut class.

---

## Image Format Analysis

All images were found to be RGB color images. No grayscale images were present in the dataset. Therefore, no color space conversion is required before model training.

---

## Image Dimension Analysis

Image dimension analysis revealed significant variation in image sizes across classes.

### Bacterial Leaf Blight

* Number of unique image sizes: 1
* Image size: (3081, 897)

All images in this class have identical dimensions, indicating a highly consistent image acquisition process.

### Brown Spot

* Number of unique image sizes: 20
* Minimum image size: (286, 92)
* Maximum image size: (3081, 897)

The Brown Spot class contains images with multiple resolutions and dimensions.

### Leaf Smut

* Number of unique image sizes: 15
* Minimum image size: (250, 200)
* Maximum image size: (3081, 897)

The Leaf Smut class also contains images with varying dimensions.

These findings indicate that image resizing is necessary during preprocessing to create a uniform input size for deep learning models.

---

## Aspect Ratio Analysis

Aspect ratio analysis was performed to understand image shape consistency.

### Bacterial Leaf Blight

* Number of unique aspect ratios: 1
* Aspect ratio: 3.43

All images have the same aspect ratio.

### Brown Spot

* Number of unique aspect ratios: 20

Images contain a wide range of aspect ratios, indicating substantial variation in image shapes.

### Leaf Smut

* Number of unique aspect ratios: 15

Images contain multiple aspect ratios and varying image shapes.

The variation in aspect ratios confirms the need for image resizing before model training.

